  "prefix": "l08e",
  "title": "A leaver keeps access: which path holds it",
  "desc": "A tree over places a leaver's access can live. An established SP session is the SP's own, and the SP SHOULD discard its security context at SessionNotOnOrAfter. For a JWT checked locally, local validation never asks the IdP, so the token is good until exp. Separately, introspection (RFC 7662) reports whether a token is active, and revocation (RFC 7009) invalidates tokens from a grant. After SCIM sets active to false, the service provider defines what that means.",
  "duration": 18,
